          "id": "body",
          "type": "text",
          "enabled": true,
          "order": 0,
          "props": {
            "body": "Beanstalk started in 2021 in a 400-square-foot Bushwick storefront with a used Diedrich roaster and a stubborn belief that coffee tastes better when you know where it came from. Five years later we work directly with twelve farms across Ethiopia, Colombia, Guatemala, Sumatra, Costa Rica, and Kenya. We pay above Fair Trade, we visit every farm at least once a year, and we publish what we paid per pound on every bag. Coffee is agriculture. We try to act like it."
          }
        }
      ],
      "content": {
        "heading": "About Beanstalk",
        "subheading": "Direct trade, transparent pricing, roasted in small batches"
      }
    },
